+# Utility-aware VPD selection follow-up
+
+Date: 2026-09-11. Status: prospective archive-only design. No model was loaded, no inference was run, no VPD or dictionary was fitted, and no edit was applied for this follow-up.
+
+## Evidence carried forward
+
+The activation-category/SAE review does not support spending capacity on separate dictionaries. Equal-total-rank pass routing earned zero admissions in 36 archive/site/rank checks: the monolithic arm won 35 and one comparison was inconclusive. A bisector fitted from the same existing packs can describe their shared geometry, but it is not transfer to a new domain and does not identify feature semantics. Loader or callback conformance establishes engineering compatibility only.
+
+The operative starting point is therefore one shared representation and a finite intervention catalog. The scientific question is whether a frozen selection rule chooses a downstream-useful candidate under equal rank and fit budget, not whether geometry looks structured.
+
+## Frozen selection comparison
+
+Three selectors act on the same sealed catalog:
+
+| Selector | Information used | Rule |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Global utility | Calibration task outcomes | Largest mean calibration utility |
+| Geometric | Discovery-only geometry | Largest frozen geometry score |
+| Interval-aware | Calibration utility and uncertainty | Smallest worst-case regret among candidates satisfying the benign-loss bound |
+
+Catalog entries are interventions, not selectors. Every entry records the exact site, direction/subspace, sign, dose, total rank, edited-coordinate accounting, fit lineage, identity certificate, and physical-cost caps. Include the unchanged baseline, the preregistered geometric candidates, at least two matched random subspaces, and a pass/site-label-only control. A failed or missing registered candidate remains an unmeasured challenger unless an outcome-independent constraint made it infeasible before reveal.
+
+The comparison matches total rank, fit model-call allowance, fit FLOP cap, fit-storage cap, edited-coordinate cap, calibration cases, and final cases. Unused allowance cannot finance extra search. Actual resource use remains visible even when caps match.
+
+## Utility and missed challengers
+
+For candidate `q`, report downstream improvement over the unchanged baseline and regret to the best reachable candidate as different estimands. If simultaneous candidate-mean intervals are `[L_p,U_p]`, use:
+
+`improvement(q) in [L_q-U_0, U_q-L_0]`
+
+`regret(q) in [max(0,max_(p!=q)(L_p-U_q)), max(0,max_(p!=q)(U_p-L_q))]`.
+
+Name every possible missed challenger and the candidates attaining each regret bound. Improvement can be positive while regret remains large. An unmeasured challenger retains `[0,1]`, usually preventing a strong regret claim; this is the intended penalty for incomplete comparison.
+
+The offline calculator uses a conservative Hoeffding/union-bound interval over all task and benign candidate means. The independent unit is a complete case family or run replicate. Tokens, activation rows, prompt variants, matched arms, and retries are not independent observations. Report the primary result at score-error radius zero and sensitivity radii 0.02 and 0.05 under the declared box error set. These radii test score misspecification; they do not establish robustness to a new domain.
+
+Direction value and site-selection value remain separate estimands within the existing identity strata. Do not pool across contrast types or identity levels. Held-out-family, matched-random, label-only, and unchanged controls are all required.
+
+## Physical access costs
+
+Record five ledgers separately:
+
+1. Model requests, forward/backward calls, recurrent invocations, retries, and generated tokens.
+2. Fit, capture, selector, and evaluation FLOPs, including the estimator and version.
+3. Persistent/read bytes, hashes, and peak RAM/VRAM.
+4. Total rank, distinct physical parameter entries, activation coordinates, repeated writes, and edit norm.
+5. Benign utility loss relative to the unchanged baseline with simultaneous uncertainty.
+
+A rank-one dense parameter update is not one edited scalar. A one-dimensional activation direction may write every hidden coordinate and may be applied at many tokens or recurrent passes. Unknown historical cost is `null` with a reason, never zero. Utility and resources stay separate rather than using a fitted post-outcome exchange rate.
+
+## Decision rule and falsifiers
+
+A result is eligible only if its simultaneous improvement lower bound is positive, regret upper bound is at most 0.02, benign-loss upper bound is at most 0.01, matched controls lose under the registered contrast, and all earlier identity/support/rank/norm/execution gates pass. Otherwise retain the unchanged baseline and current shared-monolithic interpretation.
+
+The claim is falsified or unsupported if random/label-only controls match the proposed advantage, final families influence selection, budgets differ, missing challengers disappear, or geometry/reconstruction/probe metrics substitute for task utility. No result from these existing packs alone may be promoted to semantic attribution or third-domain transfer.
+
+The machine-readable design is `protocols/vpd_utility_aware_selection_v0_1.json`. `rsi_topology.utility_selection` provides offline arithmetic for frozen block tables; it does not select a live edit or authorize execution.
